    "id": "p17-q18-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "The product of two consecutive numbers is 72. Find the numbers using a quadratic equation.\nNote that there are two possible sets of numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8$ and $9$, or $-9$ and $-8$. Solve $x(x+1)=72$ by factorising.",
      "worked": "Let the consecutive numbers be $x$ and $x+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+1)&=72\\\\x^2+x-72&=0\\\\(x+9)(x-8)&=0\\\\x&=-9\\text{ or }8\\end{align*}$$\nBy the null factor law, the numbers are $-9$ and $-8$, or $8$ and $9$.\nCheck: $(-9)(-8)=72$ and $8\\times9=72$; both pairs are consecutive.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
